WEBVTT

1
00:00:01.199 --> 00:00:06.200
Okay, so in this section we're going to review the tracking solution for the options that you have available,

2
00:00:06.200 --> 00:00:11.199
along with the plugins and system options that you have in your project.

3
00:00:11.199 --> 00:00:17.199
So first thing we want to do is we want to make sure that in virtual production in ICD-FX, our plugins are working and active.

4
00:00:17.199 --> 00:00:24.199
Now you need to make sure that if you're using OptiTrack or Vicon, any external program that you're using for your motion tracking or your performance tracking software

5
00:00:24.199 --> 00:00:29.199
needs to be downloaded and installed on every single computer that is going to be talking to each other,

6
00:00:29.199 --> 00:00:33.200
so every node for rendering needs to have all these plugins active.

7
00:00:33.200 --> 00:00:36.200
Now most of them are going to live and exist already within the engine,

8
00:00:36.200 --> 00:00:40.200
but if there are additional ones that you need, please make sure that you download them before you get started.

9
00:00:40.200 --> 00:00:45.200
Additional plugins for DMX, VR, and XR can also be enabled depending on your production needs,

10
00:00:45.200 --> 00:00:52.200
if you're going to do some live DMX lighting or some virtual scouting or any of the other tools that we have available for ICD-FX.

11
00:00:52.200 --> 00:00:58.200
Now you'll note here in blue we have the Aja Media Player, Blackmagic Media Player, Camera Calibration, LED Wall Calibration,

12
00:00:58.200 --> 00:01:03.200
OpenCV Lens Distortion, and the Live Link Camera and Live Link Lens plugins.

13
00:01:03.200 --> 00:01:09.200
Those blue plugins are specific to ICD-FX, the orange plugins are specific to virtual production,

14
00:01:09.200 --> 00:01:15.200
and the white plugins are additional virtual production plugins that are automatically active as well in the system,

15
00:01:15.200 --> 00:01:18.200
but can be enabled as options for everything else.

16
00:01:18.200 --> 00:01:22.200
Things like switchboard, ICD-FX, they all need to be enabled as you go through this.

17
00:01:22.200 --> 00:01:28.230
Now, moving on to our tracking systems as well, there are several options that you have available.

18
00:01:28.230 --> 00:01:34.230
Alate Stage that we've got here uses the OptiTrack Motive performance capture system for camera and object tracking,

19
00:01:34.230 --> 00:01:38.230
nodal point calibration, and lens distortion mapping, as we've already seen,

20
00:01:38.230 --> 00:01:44.230
but other solutions such as the Vicon Shogun and the Vive Tracker and Vive Mars systems are available as well.

21
00:01:44.230 --> 00:01:48.230
One thing to note is that your camera tracking should be active as part of your stage setup,

22
00:01:49.230 --> 00:01:54.230
and the tracking setup, including setting the origin point of 000 for your tracking volume,

23
00:01:54.230 --> 00:01:58.230
camera calibration, and lens distortion mapping are covered in this previous course.

24
00:01:58.230 --> 00:02:03.230
However, as you go through and do your calibration, you may notice that after your initial calibration,

25
00:02:03.230 --> 00:02:07.230
the tracking volume might require some daily refinement to the calibration.

26
00:02:07.230 --> 00:02:12.229
Refining the calibration should be done daily or several times a day to maintain the volume

27
00:02:12.229 --> 00:02:15.229
and prevent tracking marker drift over time.

28
00:02:15.229 --> 00:02:22.229
As you see here in these images, the OptiTrack Motive system and the Vicon Shogun system have similar tracking calibration options.

29
00:02:22.229 --> 00:02:27.229
Typically, you're going to be looking for a residual mean error of less than one millimeter,

30
00:02:27.229 --> 00:02:30.229
so 0.9, as you can see here, is a good result.

31
00:02:30.229 --> 00:02:34.229
You want to get that residual mean error to be as low as possible.

32
00:02:34.229 --> 00:02:37.229
That's going to give you a good calibration and a good tracking option.

33
00:02:37.229 --> 00:02:41.229
Unreal Engine does require the installation of the tracking system plugins.

34
00:02:41.229 --> 00:02:44.229
Just a reminder for you that on each machine that is connecting through Switchboard,

35
00:02:44.229 --> 00:02:50.229
and for any additional resources, you can just visit the websites of any of the respective tracking systems that are out there.

36
00:02:50.229 --> 00:02:52.229
So that's it for our tracking and calibration.

37
00:02:52.229 --> 00:02:58.229
Next, we're going to talk about some of the other dependencies that we're going to need for tracking our camera.
